      "message": "Learnt on this working on these test cases. \n\nI have added below comment on BZ - https://bugzilla.redhat.com/show_bug.cgi?id\u003d2415390\n\nClient runs as root → Export has root_squash → Tests fail\nExpected. Root is mapped to an unprivileged user, which cannot create device nodes or change ownership.\n\nClient runs as root → Export has no_root_squash → Tests pass\nExpected. Root retains full privileges and can perform all operations required by the tests.\n\nClient runs as non-root → Export has no_root_squash → Tests fail\nExpected. Non-root users cannot set arbitrary ownership or create special files, so these tests naturally fail.\n\n\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\n\nIf this looks all good, shall we abandon this PR?",
